<h2>1. The Two Main Routes: Tarifa vs Algeciras (Don't Make This Mistake!)</h2>

      <p>The single most catastrophic error international travelers make is confusing <strong>Tangier Ville (Tanger Ville)</strong> with <strong>Tanger Med</strong>. They are two completely different ports separated by 50 kilometers of winding highway:</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Route A: Tarifa to Tangier Ville (FRS / DFDS &amp; Baleària):</strong>
          <br>This is the gold standard for travelers. Tarifa is the southernmost tip of continental Europe. High-speed catamarans cover the 14-kilometer strait in <strong>60 minutes flat</strong>. You arrive directly at Tangier Ville port, located immediately beneath the ancient walls of the Kasbah and Medina.</li>
        <li><strong>Route B: Algeciras to Tanger Med (FRS, Baleària, AML, Trasmediterránea):</strong>
          <br>Algeciras is an industrial Spanish port city. Ferries here are large vehicle vessels that dock at <em>Tanger Med</em>, a sprawling commercial container terminal nestled near Ksar Sghir. If you arrive here as a foot passenger without pre-arranged transport, you face an exhausting, expensive 50-minute taxi ride just to reach Tangier city.</li>
      </ul>

