      <!-- Section 7: Tarifa Town Guide -->
      <h2>7. How to Reach the Port of Tarifa from Spain</h2>

      <p>Tarifa is a bohemian, whitewashed Andalusian seaside town on the Costa de la Luz. Depending on where your Spanish journey begins, here is how to get there:</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>From Seville (2.5 hours):</strong> Transportes Comes operates direct daily air-conditioned express buses from Seville (Prado de San Sebastián station) directly to Tarifa bus terminal, located 10 minutes walk from the ferry port.</li>
        <li><strong>From Málaga / Costa del Sol (2 hours):</strong> Avanza buses run from Málaga Maria Zambrano station to Algeciras. From Algeciras, FRS ferry lines provide a <strong>free shuttle bus</strong> connecting Algeciras port to Tarifa port for passengers holding valid FRS ferry tickets.</li>
        <li><strong>From Algeciras Train Station (Renfe):</strong> If taking the scenic Renfe train from Madrid or Ronda down to Algeciras, take a 10-minute taxi to Algeciras port and board the complimentary FRS ferry shuttle bus to Tarifa.</li>
      </ul>

