      <!-- Section 8: FAQ Accordion -->
      <h2>8. Frequently Asked Questions About the Spain-to-Morocco Ferry</h2>

      <div class="faq-accordion">
        <div class="faq-item active">
          <h3 class="faq-question">How long does the ferry from Spain to Morocco take?</h3>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>The high-speed passenger catamaran from <strong>Tarifa to Tangier Ville takes exactly 60 minutes</strong> across the water. The conventional ferry from <strong>Algeciras to Tanger Med takes between 90 and 120 minutes</strong>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">What happens if the ferry is cancelled due to high winds (Levante)?</h3>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>The Strait of Gibraltar is prone to fierce easterly winds known as the <em>Levante</em>. When winds exceed safety thresholds, the Port of Tarifa may suspend fast catamaran sailings. In this rare event, ferry companies automatically transfer passengers onto large roll-on/roll-off vehicle vessels departing from the protected harbor of <strong>Algeciras to Tanger Med</strong>. Our private chauffeur dispatch automatically adjusts pickup logistics to meet you at Tanger Med at no extra inconvenience.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">Do I need a visa to take the ferry to Morocco?</h3>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Citizens of the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and European Union nations do not need a visa for tourist visits to Morocco for stays up to 90 days. You only need a valid passport with at least 6 months validity remaining.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">How much luggage can I bring on the ferry?</h3>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Unlike airlines, ferry operators (FRS and Baleària) do not weigh or limit standard passenger luggage. Foot passengers are allowed to bring large suitcases, rolling bags, backpacks, and personal items free of charge. You carry your bags onto the vessel and store them in luggage racks in the passenger lounge.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">Can I exchange currency or get Moroccan Dirhams at Tangier port?</h3>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Yes. The passenger arrival terminal at Tangier Ville port features multiple bank currency exchange windows and bank ATMs (distributeurs de billets) where you can withdraw Moroccan Dirhams (MAD) using international debit cards. We recommend withdrawing 500 to 1,000 MAD for small tips and snacks before starting your overland drive.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
